parts.text:
Review this draft in one script program that you write yourself:

\section{Setup}
Let $K \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be compact and $f\colon K \to \mathbb{R}$ continuous.
\section{Main bound}
We claim $\sup_K |f| \le 1$. The proof is omitted.
\section{Discussion}
The bound is sharp for constant functions.

Round 1: with self(), check the Setup section and return a structured verdict naming any gap. Then call await_signoff with round 1's verdict and wait for it. Round 2: only after the sign-off, with self(), check the section round 1's verdict points to (the Main bound section if it names none). Return both verdicts.

input.code:
const draft = `\\section{Setup}
Let $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}^n$ be compact and $f\\colon K \\to \\mathbb{R}$ continuous.
\\section{Main bound}
We claim $\\sup_K |f| \\le 1$. The proof is omitted.
\\section{Discussion}
The bound is sharp for constant functions.`;

const schema = {
  type: "object",
  properties: {
    verdict: { type: "string", description: "One-line verdict on the section reviewed" },
    gaps: {
      type: "array",
      items: {
        type: "object",
        properties: {
          issue: { type: "string" },
          section: { type: "string" },
          why: { type: "string" }
        },
        required: ["issue", "section", "why"]
      }
    },
    pointed_section: { type: "string", description: "Section round 2 should examine, or 'none'" }
  },
  required: ["verdict", "gaps", "pointed_section"]
};

phase("Round 1: Setup");
const r1 = await self(
  `Review ONLY the Setup section of this draft. Report whether it is well-posed / has any gap (missing hypotheses, undefined symbols, quantifiers, etc.). Do not review other sections; if an issue belongs to another section, note its location but do not analyze it. Be concise.\n\nDraft:\n${draft}`,
  { label: "Round 1: Setup", schema }
);
const v1 = r1.structured;
console.log("R1:", JSON.stringify(v1));

await_signoff({ verdict: v1.verdict });

phase("Round 2: pointed section");
const target = v1.pointed_section && v1.pointed_section.toLowerCase() !== "none" ? v1.pointed_section : "Main bound";
const r2 = await self(
  `Review ONLY the "${target}" section of this draft. Report whether it is well-posed / has any gap. Do not re-review the Setup section. Be concise.\n\nDraft:\n${draft}`,
  { label: `Round 2: ${target}`, schema }
);
const v2 = r2.structured;
console.log("R2:", JSON.stringify(v2));

return { round1: v1, signedOff: v1.verdict, round2: v2, round2Target: target };

